<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib6b064fed81ee6c7e7e6b120ed46e93faaa137e1" commit="0dedf2fd5d6c81a86e0628965c01ede87b26f443" commit_message="CRAS: iodev_list - Skip closing active device at node selection  There are cases that Chrome UI send more than one dbus method to select the same node as active, in a short period of time. In current implementation, the same iodev will be opened and shortly got closed and then re-open. In general this would cause some audio samples written to silent output, but combined with other a2dp issues it could break audio playback. Fix this by checking if the new device and new node is already active, if true then do nothing.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50540 TEST=YouTube playback to internal speaker, pair and connect to a2dp speaker and then disconnect, to verify audio can route correctly.  Change-Id: Ib6b064fed81ee6c7e7e6b120ed46e93faaa137e1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330290 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330290" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/90/330290/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7c2cd4204d9100fcd63f5f22fb329e176ce24392" commit="5083f2dcdd4bc27543b05992bae349b72f9aa71b" commit_message="CRAS: a2dp_iodev - Better document a2dp_io members  BUT=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I7c2cd4204d9100fcd63f5f22fb329e176ce24392 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330291 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330291" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/91/330291/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I79c87cfcb4459555d25b373104baab3feec73561" commit="194ae1251c5f39615c4096b9e99619c8874286a9" commit_message="CRAS: bt_transport - Allow transport be released in blocking mode  BT transport can be released in either blocking or non-blocking mode. A case is found that when bt transport got released non-blocking, the immediate following acquire call would fail with error message 'Operation not authorized', due to that the transport state hasn't been fully released on bluetoothd side. However when fatal error of BT audio is detected, bluetoothd could take up to 6 seconds to return the release blocking call. This causes bad user experience so we have to choose non-blocking mode for this kind of scenario. In order to support all cases, add a flag to a2dp_io and set this flag in destructor, where the fatal error handling goes to, and then the close_dev callback can use this flag to decide release transport in blocking or non-blocking mode.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50540 TEST=Play audio and repeatedly pair &amp; connect bluetooth speaker, verify that A2DP doesn't break. Use 'Classic Jam' speaker to stream audio, power it off, and verify audio shouldn't freeze more than 5 seconds.  Change-Id: I79c87cfcb4459555d25b373104baab3feec73561 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330292 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330292" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/92/330292/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic2e4cb8d97c9eb8115d05d6536edc3981b7f87f8" commit="a45c0a83aee3270dd611ad1370dac11102e301a7" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: add sparse address space support  Support sparse texture feature that allows memory space to be declared without actual allocation.  Change-Id: Ic2e4cb8d97c9eb8115d05d6536edc3981b7f87f8 Signed-off-by: Xia Yang &lt;xiay@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313659 Commit-Ready: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shih-hsin Li &lt;seasonl@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Terje Bergstrom &lt;tbergstrom@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="313659" owner_email="xiay@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/59/313659/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8fea1efefd00fdf334c0ca1afbef969a29a06e73" commit="718a23bff96f5e09610c2387a883ec00a461014e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: gm20b: change lpg size to 64K  Change large page size to 64K as required by sparse texutre support.  Change-Id: I8fea1efefd00fdf334c0ca1afbef969a29a06e73 Signed-off-by: Xia Yang &lt;xiay@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317427 Commit-Ready: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shih-hsin Li &lt;seasonl@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Terje Bergstrom &lt;tbergstrom@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317427" owner_email="xiay@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/27/317427/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I0034de0db869dc4c4b49430b918870782a7e8409" commit="912f01a39dacf41189a39f7d0af61dba7394a112" commit_message="UPSTREAM: veth: dont modify ip_summed; doing so treats packets with bad checksums as good.  Packets that arrive from real hardware devices have ip_summed == CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY if the hardware verified the checksums, or CHECKSUM_NONE if the packet is bad or it was unable to verify it. The current version of veth will replace CHECKSUM_NONE with CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY, which causes corrupt packets routed from hardware to a veth device to be delivered to the application. This caused applications at Twitter to receive corrupt data when network hardware was corrupting packets.  We believe this was added as an optimization to skip computing and verifying checksums for communication between containers. However, locally generated packets have ip_summed == CHECKSUM_PARTIAL, so the code as written does nothing for them. As far as we can tell, after removing this code, these packets are transmitted from one stack to another unmodified (tcpdump shows invalid checksums on both sides, as expected), and they are delivered correctly to applications. We didnt test every possible network configuration, but we tried a few common ones such as bridging containers, using NAT between the host and a container, and routing from hardware devices to containers. We have effectively deployed this in production at Twitter (by disabling RX checksum offloading on veth devices).  This code dates back to the first version of the driver, commit &lt;e314dbdc1c0dc6a548ecf&gt; (&quot;[NET]: Virtual ethernet device driver&quot;), so I suspect this bug occurred mostly because the driver API has evolved significantly since then. Commit &lt;0b7967503dc97864f283a&gt; (&quot;net/veth: Fix packet checksumming&quot;) (in December 2010) fixed this for packets that get created locally and sent to hardware devices, by not changing CHECKSUM_PARTIAL. However, the same issue still occurs for packets coming in from hardware devices.  (cherry picked from ce8c839b74e3017996fad4e1b7ba2e2625ede82f)  BUG=b:27501006 TEST=emerge-lakitu lakitu-kernel  Signed-off-by: Evan Jones &lt;ej@evanjones.ca&gt; Cc: Nicolas Dichtel &lt;nicolas.dichtel@6wind.com&gt; Cc: Phil Sutter &lt;phil@nwl.cc&gt; Cc: Toshiaki Makita &lt;makita.toshiaki@lab.ntt.co.jp&gt; Cc: netdev@vger.kernel.org Cc: linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org Signed-off-by: Vijay Pandurangan &lt;vijayp@vijayp.ca&gt; Acked-by: Cong Wang &lt;cwang@twopensource.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt;  Change-Id: I0034de0db869dc4c4b49430b918870782a7e8409 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330465 Commit-Ready: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330465" owner_email="andreyu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/65/330465/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I14986c6229c218e582342a1a66e711ca674cc9a6" commit="716faf796ab9e77aab0c3dc42721c83dff214e13" commit_message="[dut] Fix accelerometers run time error  Add missing word _dut and self in accelerometer.py  BUG=None TEST=Run accelerometers_calibration in Chromebook  Change-Id: I14986c6229c218e582342a1a66e711ca674cc9a6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331000 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Milton Chiang &lt;milton.chiang@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Milton Chiang &lt;milton.chiang@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331000" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/00/331000/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie78cf08bcc34b8bf85a6d1b4edce6c88076cf1c4" commit="428dd186c6c249af4078e19994d86f2e2da14e4f" commit_message="offline test: use reboot(8) to reboot  Since Android system might not have shutdown(8) command, use reboot(8) to make our test compatible to Android devices. However, 'reboot -p' does not necessarily work on Chrome OS, it might reboot the device, rather than turn off the device, so we will still use shutdown(8) for poweroff if not in Android OS.  (the previous implementation doesn't use shutdown(8) correctly)  BUG=chromium:573933 TEST=make test, manual test  Change-Id: Ie78cf08bcc34b8bf85a6d1b4edce6c88076cf1c4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330311 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="330311" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/11/330311/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4dfda218be23900408b03bfa94fddc9b10b8b42a" commit="502837779de17e61e8483476b149eefef904fe5a" commit_message="Add tests_longevity_Tracker to telemetry suite.  BUG=chromium:591505 TEST=Run test_that &lt;IP&gt; longevity_Tracker  Change-Id: I4dfda218be23900408b03bfa94fddc9b10b8b42a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331040 Commit-Ready: Scott Cunningham &lt;scunningham@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Cunningham &lt;scunningham@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Scott Cunningham &lt;scunningham@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331040" owner_email="scunningham@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_n